"""Mutations of part 8a's world modules (src/game/vertex_anim.*, lightmap_groups.*, tshift.*) for
../mutfast.py with the world build:

    python mutfast.py mutations/mutate_8a.py --models DIR --build build_world.bat --check check_world.py

DIR holds a .txt per mission ("mission NAME"). Each mutation should make check_world.py fail (or the
harness crash / hang). Generated from the sources (a comparison, a number, an operator or a
statement per line), then pruned. Left out as equivalent (30): the distance's exact 1e-8 square
(a frame that close is near either way) and its exact-1 shortcut (sqrt gives the same 1); leaks
(the animation's arrays, a group not deleted, the last frame or level not freed, a frame array one
longer); a read that gets a single byte, which only the file's end gives, so the next read fails
the same way (the def's name, counts, vertex counts and vertices, the bin's level, start frame
and frame time); the server flag of the StartMission / RestartMission calls (not read); header
defaults that are set again (the animation's last frame and level count, the player's frame, next
frame, time and distance, m_started). 5 more did not compile (deleted special members and
inline bodies) and were dropped.

Results (2026-10-30): the first run caught 233 of 287 (5 did not compile, 49 survived); of the 49,
30 equivalent (above) and 19 with new cases (the ping-pong turns away from the end, a sort at
exactly 300 ms, dtaOpen's flag, a player listed twice and one removed already, a level past the
animation's, the distance exactly 1 and 0 under wide views, a version-0 record cut one byte into
its animation's name, the empty-named frame that unread names find, SaveGame / LoadGame's
results). Regenerated with TShift's five functions: the rerun caught 265 of 267; the 2 left (the
zeroed fields of AddVisual's entry) went with the header's defaults. All 265 caught.
"""
